From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:05:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] misc: add an FPC1264 sensor control driver for liuqin

Add the control side of the FPC1264 fingerprint sensor on the Xiaomi
Pad 6 Pro: VDD supply, active-low reset, the finger-detect interrupt
and a /dev/fpc1020 misc device. Opening the device powers the sensor
and the last close powers it down; poll() reports the finger
interrupt. Enrolment and matching run in the OEM trusted application
(fpcliu) reached through the QSEECOM TEE driver, not here. The
fpc,fpc1020 compatible and the /dev/fpc1020 name are kept as the
existing interface names; only the FPC1264 on this tablet has been
exercised.

Changes from the submitted driver:
 - read() and write() now refuse transfers above 64 KiB, the same bound
   SPI_IOC_MESSAGE segments already had, instead of letting a caller
   size a kernel allocation;
 - FPC_IOC_RESET takes the power lock and only toggles reset on a
   powered sensor, so it cannot race suspend or a concurrent open.

The driver is meant to be built as a module (SENSORS_FPC1020_SPI=m).

Co-developed-by: reisa <reisa8366@gmail.com>
Based-on: https://github.com/yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin/pull/7 (yuzelingsha)
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

